side. Some revolutions are just remembering, together."}, {'n': 4, 'title': 'The Remembering', 'text': "By dawn the Patrol had stood down — human, after all, and shown the same thirty seconds. the Overseer was gone by noon, the Algorithm's servers dark. the Glass District belonged to its people again. It had only ever been on loan.\n\nan offline map burned out in the broadcast — one use, that was the price. Nyx Carter held the dead chip and didn't mourn it. Seeds die to grow. That was the whole point.\n\nthe Overseer responded the only way the Overseer knew: force. The Patrol marched. The drones rose. And the people of the Glass District — who had just remembered green, and laughter, and sky — stood in the streets and would not move."}, {'n': 5, 'title': 'After the Static', 'text': "The footage from an offline map became the Glass District's founding document: not a constitution, but a memory. This is what we were. This is what we can be. small sparks burn bright — carved, at the hacker Jinx's insistence, over the tower door.\n\nRebuilding the Glass District was harder than freeing it. Nyx Carter organized food lines with the same care once used for heists. the hacker Jinx taught kids to code on salvaged terminals. The medic ran a clinic. The runner ran messages of hope.\n\nThere were trials. the Overseer's people faced justice — real justice, not the Algorithm's kind, with evidence and mercy both. Some were guilty. Some were just afraid. Nyx Carter learned the difference matters."}, {'n': 6, 'title': 'The Habit of Freedom', 'text': "And somewhere, in a gutter where drones don't look, someone is finding something warm that shouldn't be warm. It starts again. It always starts again. That's the best part.\n\nthe hacker Jinx runs the network now — the real one, the open one, the one that belongs to everyone. The rebuild is quieter. The neon is warmer. It turns out freedom has a sound, and it's laughter.\n\nsmall sparks burn bright — Nyx Carter thinks it every time, lik